1
00:00:01,001 --> 00:00:03,336
[theme music playing]

2
00:00:03,420 --> 00:00:06,464
[tense music playing]

3
00:00:20,353 --> 00:00:21,646
[screaming]

4
00:00:21,730 --> 00:00:23,773
[shattering sound]

5
00:00:27,402 --> 00:00:29,612
<i>Say your prayers</i>
<i>because you're about to die.</i>

6
00:00:29,696 --> 00:00:31,239
[Damian] <i>I'm sorry.</i>
<i>I didn't want to do this.</i>

7
00:00:31,322 --> 00:00:33,700
[Raul] <i>Let Diego go!</i>
<i>He has nothing to do with this!</i>

8
00:00:33,783 --> 00:00:36,494
-[gunshots]
-[groans]

9
00:00:38,121 --> 00:00:39,622
<i>Dad? You're the Jaguar?</i>

10
00:00:39,706 --> 00:00:42,208
[Raul] <i>I only wear that mask</i>
<i>to guarantee your safety,</i>

11
00:00:42,292 --> 00:00:43,543
<i>to keep you from danger.</i>

12
00:00:43,626 --> 00:00:46,129
<i>To keep you safe from Red Dragon.</i>

13
00:00:46,212 --> 00:00:48,381
[Diego] <i>This is the key</i>
<i>to Red Dragon's world.</i>

14
00:00:48,465 --> 00:00:51,426
[Lily] <i>I'll catch you, Mercedes Palacio.</i>

15
00:00:51,509 --> 00:00:53,636
<i>-Are you okay?</i>
<i>-I'm sorry. Yes.</i>

16
00:00:54,971 --> 00:00:56,598
[man] <i>The keycard. I think I lost it.</i>

17
00:00:56,681 --> 00:00:58,183
<i>Mercedes, I can't reach you</i>
<i>on your cellphone.</i>

18
00:00:58,266 --> 00:01:00,894
<i>I've been trying to call you.</i>
<i>You need to report to me, ASAP.</i>

19
00:01:00,977 --> 00:01:03,855
[Lily] <i>Helena Montoya as Red Dragon.</i>

20
00:01:04,522 --> 00:01:06,900
<i>And now, my enemy finally has a face.</i>

21
00:01:06,983 --> 00:01:08,568
[Emilia] <i>I'm sure whoever</i>
<i>was on the other line</i>

22
00:01:08,651 --> 00:01:09,652
<i>plans to take you down.</i>

23
00:01:09,736 --> 00:01:11,821
[Helena] <i>Anyone that battles a dragon</i>

24
00:01:11,905 --> 00:01:14,074
<i>should be ready to die in a blaze.</i>

25
00:01:14,157 --> 00:01:16,785
[Lily] <i>I need stronger evidence.</i>
<i>Then she'll go to prison</i>

26
00:01:16,868 --> 00:01:21,081
<i>and pay for what she did to Aguas Realty.</i>

27
00:01:21,164 --> 00:01:23,541
-[Diego] <i>I've got an idea.</i>
-[Lily] <i>I trust you.</i>

28
00:01:23,625 --> 00:01:25,418
[Diego] <i>I can infiltrate</i>
<i>Red Dragon's hideout.</i>

29
00:01:25,835 --> 00:01:27,796
[Emilia] <i>I'm sure, you'll have</i>
<i>even more fun now</i>

30
00:01:27,879 --> 00:01:31,341
<i>because Emilia Ardiente Torillo is here,</i>

31
00:01:31,424 --> 00:01:34,052
<i>the only daughter of Helena Montoya.</i>

32
00:01:34,135 --> 00:01:36,930
[Lily] <i>I can't go on with this project</i>

33
00:01:37,013 --> 00:01:39,641
<i>if your daughter, Emilia, meddles in.</i>

34
00:01:40,141 --> 00:01:42,310
<i>-Helena!</i>
-[metal clanks]

35
00:01:42,685 --> 00:01:43,812
<i>-Are you okay?</i>
<i>-Yeah.</i>

36
00:01:43,895 --> 00:01:45,897
<i>Are you sure? You might have an injury.</i>

37
00:01:52,654 --> 00:01:54,739
Mama! Move it!

38
00:01:54,823 --> 00:01:56,533
Stay away! Mama.

39
00:01:56,616 --> 00:01:57,784
-Lily.
-Mama.

40
00:01:57,867 --> 00:01:59,327
-Lily.
-Mama, are you okay?

41
00:01:59,410 --> 00:02:00,745
-Yeah, I'm fine.
-Were you hurt?

42
00:02:02,956 --> 00:02:05,875
-Lily dear, are you hurt?
-No, I'm fine.

43
00:02:05,959 --> 00:02:07,877
Lily, don't ever do that again, okay?

44
00:02:09,003 --> 00:02:11,256
-I'm sorry.
-Come here.

45
00:02:14,759 --> 00:02:16,719
[pensive music playing]

46
00:02:33,945 --> 00:02:35,238
-Jepoy.
-Yes?

47
00:02:35,321 --> 00:02:38,241
What did you mean when you said
Lily needed an ally?

48
00:02:38,992 --> 00:02:41,119
Do you know someone
who wants to help Lily?

49
00:02:41,578 --> 00:02:42,370
I do.

50
00:02:42,954 --> 00:02:43,997
Who?

51
00:02:46,291 --> 00:02:49,502
<i>I want to help Lily.</i>

52
00:02:49,919 --> 00:02:51,629
<i>In her fight against the Ardientes.</i>

53
00:02:51,880 --> 00:02:54,173
<i>It's going to be a tactical alliance.</i>

54
00:02:54,799 --> 00:02:57,760
<i>It should've been like</i>
<i>that a long time ago</i>

55
00:02:57,844 --> 00:02:59,762
<i>since we have the same enemies.</i>

56
00:03:02,390 --> 00:03:03,975
Someone does want to help Lily.

57
00:03:04,809 --> 00:03:06,686
But you wouldn't like it
if I told you who,

58
00:03:06,769 --> 00:03:08,021
so… never mind.

59
00:03:08,396 --> 00:03:09,689
Who is it?

60
00:03:11,566 --> 00:03:14,027
-Do you really want to know?
-Why can't you say it?

61
00:03:16,195 --> 00:03:17,030
It's Natalie.

62
00:03:17,530 --> 00:03:20,366
Natalie? Are you serious, Jepoy?

63
00:03:20,450 --> 00:03:22,243
You actually trust that woman?

64
00:03:23,745 --> 00:03:25,914
And you plan on telling Lily that?

65
00:03:26,873 --> 00:03:27,957
I don't get it, Anna.

66
00:03:28,917 --> 00:03:31,920
You're so convinced that someone
like Arnaldo can change.

67
00:03:32,003 --> 00:03:35,632
But now that Natalie wants to
help us, you think it's wrong.

68
00:03:35,715 --> 00:03:37,175
I don't get you either.

69
00:03:37,258 --> 00:03:40,136
You've seen that Arnaldo has changed,
but you can't accept it.

70
00:03:40,220 --> 00:03:41,095
I don't buy it.

71
00:03:41,179 --> 00:03:43,890
But it's so easy for you to trust Natalie!

72
00:03:43,973 --> 00:03:47,227
Probably 'cause you aren't
thinking with your head.

73
00:03:50,897 --> 00:03:54,484
[tense music playing]

74
00:04:04,827 --> 00:04:07,872
[pensive music playing]

75
00:04:32,814 --> 00:04:33,856
Sir.

76
00:04:35,316 --> 00:04:37,568
Should I go fetch Madam Helena?

77
00:04:41,239 --> 00:04:42,240
[thud]

78
00:04:45,952 --> 00:04:47,745
Helena Montoya…

79
00:04:49,414 --> 00:04:51,291
is a bloodsucking leech!

80
00:04:53,084 --> 00:04:54,419
To think…

81
00:04:56,004 --> 00:04:58,006
to think that… that woman,

82
00:04:58,965 --> 00:05:02,760
that red-faced woman
would have the decency

83
00:05:04,137 --> 00:05:05,513
to face me!

84
00:05:09,559 --> 00:05:10,560
[scoffs]

85
00:05:11,728 --> 00:05:13,313
She's not going to come back here.

86
00:05:13,896 --> 00:05:15,815
And if she does, I'm sure that…

87
00:05:16,190 --> 00:05:18,401
it's for one thing, and one thing alone.

88
00:05:19,027 --> 00:05:23,990
She'd like to swallow me whole
and chew me into little pieces

89
00:05:24,782 --> 00:05:30,913
and spit me out like
an overused chewing gum.

90
00:05:32,915 --> 00:05:33,916
[exhales sharply]

91
00:05:36,794 --> 00:05:38,087
Helena… Helena…

92
00:05:41,215 --> 00:05:42,800
The only woman…

93
00:05:43,968 --> 00:05:46,220
who can make my blood curdle

94
00:05:46,304 --> 00:05:48,598
and make me look stupid!

95
00:05:50,391 --> 00:05:53,478
This should not, this will not,

96
00:05:54,937 --> 00:05:58,608
this must not happen again!

97
00:06:01,486 --> 00:06:02,361
[thuds]

98
00:06:06,949 --> 00:06:08,367
Relax, Julio. Relax.

99
00:06:10,119 --> 00:06:16,167
She's not worth getting all worked up for.

100
00:06:19,837 --> 00:06:22,298
Relax. [exhales]

101
00:06:22,799 --> 00:06:23,966
Relax.

102
00:06:28,721 --> 00:06:30,223
Damn you, Helena!

103
00:06:30,807 --> 00:06:32,767
[slow tense music playing]

104
00:06:47,990 --> 00:06:49,117
What was that all about?

105
00:06:50,451 --> 00:06:51,828
Natalie just wanted to help

106
00:06:51,911 --> 00:06:53,412
but she went and got all mad like that.

107
00:06:53,496 --> 00:06:54,789
Wha--What's her problem?

108
00:06:54,872 --> 00:06:56,874
[phone ringing]

109
00:07:02,964 --> 00:07:04,715
She's getting me in trouble with Anna.

110
00:07:08,469 --> 00:07:10,221
[phone continues ringing]

111
00:07:16,686 --> 00:07:19,397
Ma'am, where are you? We need to talk.

112
00:07:24,318 --> 00:07:27,363
Mom, just wait for me here.

113
00:07:28,739 --> 00:07:31,159
I'll just go check on the dragon
and her daughter.

114
00:07:32,243 --> 00:07:33,244
Lily…

115
00:07:35,037 --> 00:07:36,706
Mom, let me do this.

116
00:07:38,416 --> 00:07:41,961
I'll just give them
a taste of what's to come.

117
00:07:46,382 --> 00:07:47,592
I'll be right back.

118
00:07:48,968 --> 00:07:49,969
Helena?

119
00:07:51,304 --> 00:07:53,556
-Lily.
-How are you? Doc, how is she?

120
00:07:54,182 --> 00:07:56,142
Should I take her to the hospital?

121
00:07:56,225 --> 00:07:57,143
-No need.
-Or anything?

122
00:07:57,226 --> 00:07:58,352
-Lily.
-Are you sure?

123
00:07:58,936 --> 00:08:01,105
Who died and made you daughter
of the year?

124
00:08:01,189 --> 00:08:02,857
Stop acting like you're close to my mama!

125
00:08:04,358 --> 00:08:05,401
It's over the top!

126
00:08:06,777 --> 00:08:08,654
Emilia, stop it. Please.

127
00:08:10,698 --> 00:08:12,158
You know what, Emilia?

128
00:08:12,450 --> 00:08:16,954
You're very lucky that
you reunited with your mother.

129
00:08:17,663 --> 00:08:19,123
And about what I did earlier,

130
00:08:19,707 --> 00:08:23,586
I want you to know
that I didn't regret saving her.

131
00:08:25,755 --> 00:08:27,840
Shouldn't you be thanking me, instead?

132
00:08:27,924 --> 00:08:29,175
Oh, knock it off!

133
00:08:31,135 --> 00:08:32,220
[sighs] As usual…

134
00:08:33,095 --> 00:08:35,056
Good thing you're my friend, Helena.

135
00:08:36,015 --> 00:08:38,643
Anyway, can I ask you a favor?

136
00:08:39,519 --> 00:08:40,811
Yeah. Sure.

137
00:08:41,771 --> 00:08:42,772
What is it?

138
00:08:45,107 --> 00:08:47,610
Like I said before,
I feel at ease with you.

139
00:08:48,611 --> 00:08:50,488
I want you to know that anytime,

140
00:08:51,948 --> 00:08:53,157
you can call me.

141
00:08:54,075 --> 00:08:56,494
Remember what I told you
when we had lunch?

142
00:08:56,577 --> 00:08:58,996
You're like the glamorous mother
I never had.

143
00:08:59,956 --> 00:09:00,998
Remember?

144
00:09:03,251 --> 00:09:04,252
So…

145
00:09:04,502 --> 00:09:06,712
if it's all right with you
and you don't mind…

146
00:09:07,213 --> 00:09:08,881
I want to call you Mama.

147
00:09:13,219 --> 00:09:15,388
You think it's okay?

148
00:09:17,848 --> 00:09:19,016
But, of course!

149
00:09:19,100 --> 00:09:22,061
You can call me Mama. Baby girl.

150
00:09:24,272 --> 00:09:25,231
[chuckles]

151
00:09:25,314 --> 00:09:27,525
Thank you! Thank you, Mama.

152
00:09:30,236 --> 00:09:31,279
You're…

153
00:09:33,948 --> 00:09:35,950
[tense music playing]

154
00:09:39,662 --> 00:09:42,999
I'm so happy that you're
calling me baby girl!

155
00:09:43,541 --> 00:09:46,335
You're so sweet, Helena. I mean, Mama.

156
00:09:47,211 --> 00:09:48,421
You're so sweet!

157
00:09:49,839 --> 00:09:51,674
And so are you.

158
00:09:52,925 --> 00:09:54,927
[tense music swells]

159
00:09:55,386 --> 00:09:56,512
That's enough!

160
00:09:56,596 --> 00:09:57,555
Mama, let's go.

161
00:09:57,638 --> 00:09:59,098
-You're okay now, right?
-Yeah.

162
00:10:03,477 --> 00:10:06,022
Remember, Mama, you can call me anytime.

163
00:10:06,897 --> 00:10:07,982
Yes, I will.

164
00:10:14,572 --> 00:10:17,283
Mercedes, gather our best men.

165
00:10:17,575 --> 00:10:19,827
The arms shipment
with Mr. Yi will push through.

166
00:10:21,078 --> 00:10:22,455
All right. Bye.

167
00:10:26,834 --> 00:10:28,502
Is everything good?

168
00:10:29,712 --> 00:10:30,921
That's great to hear.

169
00:10:31,797 --> 00:10:34,216
Oh! Baby girl!

170
00:10:34,925 --> 00:10:37,011
-Oh, Mama!
-What are you still doing here?

171
00:10:37,094 --> 00:10:39,430
Oh, I didn't see you there. Um…

172
00:10:40,222 --> 00:10:41,766
Let's go home together.

173
00:10:42,850 --> 00:10:44,977
You know… I still don't know

174
00:10:45,061 --> 00:10:47,688
how I can thank you enough
for saving my life.

175
00:10:49,315 --> 00:10:50,524
[clicks tongue] Mama…

176
00:10:51,525 --> 00:10:53,319
It was just a coincidence
that I was there.

177
00:10:53,402 --> 00:10:56,572
Anyone would've saved you.

178
00:10:57,948 --> 00:11:03,829
Honestly, I can sense that you
are a very good person.

179
00:11:04,497 --> 00:11:07,958
You continue to amaze me every day!

180
00:11:09,877 --> 00:11:12,129
How can I ever repay you, Lily?

181
00:11:15,633 --> 00:11:16,634
A hug?

182
00:11:18,302 --> 00:11:19,470
-Sure.
-Mama.

183
00:11:21,889 --> 00:11:24,892
[tense music playing]

184
00:11:38,406 --> 00:11:39,490
Thank you, Doctor.

185
00:11:41,075 --> 00:11:42,076
And you!

186
00:11:42,952 --> 00:11:44,829
This is your daughter's fault!

187
00:11:45,204 --> 00:11:47,248
If she hadn't left,
Mama wouldn't have followed her.

188
00:11:47,331 --> 00:11:48,833
Look what almost happened!

189
00:11:48,916 --> 00:11:52,002
Say whatever you want to, Emilia,

190
00:11:52,586 --> 00:11:54,004
but that's not how I see it.

191
00:11:54,797 --> 00:11:55,840
Oh really?

192
00:11:56,257 --> 00:11:58,968
Aren't you jealous, Camia?

193
00:11:59,051 --> 00:12:02,888
Your daughter's already
cozying up to my mother.

194
00:12:02,972 --> 00:12:06,058
You heard her. She calls my mom "Mama."

195
00:12:06,559 --> 00:12:08,018
Doesn't it make you wonder

196
00:12:08,102 --> 00:12:10,771
if she would risk her life for you too?

197
00:12:13,023 --> 00:12:15,609
Nothing really beats
your desperation, Emilia.

198
00:12:16,944 --> 00:12:19,572
You're even taking
your insecurities out on me.

199
00:12:20,197 --> 00:12:21,949
And to answer your question: Yes.

200
00:12:22,825 --> 00:12:25,077
My daughter would risk her life for me.

201
00:12:25,786 --> 00:12:27,788
She lived as Ivy Aguas.

202
00:12:27,872 --> 00:12:30,958
She was buried alive
and came back as Lily Cruz.

203
00:12:31,834 --> 00:12:32,960
What about you, Emilia?

204
00:12:34,211 --> 00:12:37,923
Can you sacrifice to that extent
for your own mother?

205
00:12:40,050 --> 00:12:42,052
[tense music playing]

206
00:13:13,626 --> 00:13:16,420
I did what you wanted me to do. That's it.

207
00:13:17,880 --> 00:13:22,092
I can't join your operations.
I need to focus on my group.

208
00:13:23,093 --> 00:13:25,429
That'd be fine if you
accomplished your mission.

209
00:13:25,971 --> 00:13:28,265
But Diego Torillo is still alive!

210
00:13:31,435 --> 00:13:32,770
Quite forgetful, aren't we?

211
00:13:33,312 --> 00:13:36,357
I kept telling you
that Diego Torillo escaped.

212
00:13:36,941 --> 00:13:39,568
We looked for him
everywhere too, but he's gone.

213
00:13:41,445 --> 00:13:43,781
So, you admit you're a failure?

214
00:13:44,782 --> 00:13:45,741
[guns click]

215
00:13:49,995 --> 00:13:51,455
Keep this in mind, Jaguar:

216
00:13:51,997 --> 00:13:54,875
If you don't show up
to the operation later,

217
00:13:55,334 --> 00:13:57,044
this bullet will lodge itself

218
00:13:57,127 --> 00:14:00,130
in the head of your beloved Camia.

219
00:14:00,464 --> 00:14:03,384
[tense music playing]

220
00:14:31,954 --> 00:14:34,957
[suspenseful music playing]

221
00:14:42,756 --> 00:14:45,593
[Helena] <i>Mercedes, gather our best men.</i>

222
00:14:45,968 --> 00:14:48,095
<i>The arms shipment with Mr. Yi</i>
<i>will push through.</i>

223
00:14:54,685 --> 00:14:55,603
Lily?

224
00:14:55,686 --> 00:14:56,687
<i>Diego?</i>

225
00:14:56,770 --> 00:14:58,147
It's confirmed.

226
00:14:58,731 --> 00:15:01,609
Red Dragon is making a shipment tonight.

227
00:15:01,692 --> 00:15:02,776
Where are you?

228
00:15:02,860 --> 00:15:04,236
<i>Give me the address.</i>

229
00:15:04,612 --> 00:15:06,530
I'll sabotage their delivery.

230
00:15:06,864 --> 00:15:10,409
[tense music playing]

231
00:15:24,715 --> 00:15:27,843
[suspenseful music playing]

232
00:15:49,239 --> 00:15:51,450
[Lily] <i>This will all come</i>
<i>to an end, Diego.</i>

233
00:15:51,951 --> 00:15:54,662
<i>We'll be free from all this</i>

234
00:15:55,245 --> 00:15:56,455
<i>and live in peace.</i>

235
00:15:56,956 --> 00:15:57,998
<i>But for now,</i>

236
00:15:58,958 --> 00:16:00,626
<i>we've got a fight on our hands.</i>

237
00:16:11,345 --> 00:16:14,723
[Diego] <i>Forgive me, Dad.</i>
<i>But I have to do this.</i>

238
00:16:32,074 --> 00:16:32,908
Lily.

239
00:16:34,451 --> 00:16:35,953
Mom, try not to worry.

240
00:16:37,579 --> 00:16:42,418
Diego said he'll help carry out
all of my plans.

241
00:16:43,627 --> 00:16:49,216
Lily, I know just how hard and
dangerous this fight of ours is.

242
00:16:50,718 --> 00:16:53,345
But I also know how brave,

243
00:16:54,638 --> 00:16:56,140
skilled, and intelligent you are.

244
00:16:56,223 --> 00:16:58,225
I know you can handle yourself.

245
00:16:58,934 --> 00:17:00,936
[soft piano music playing]

246
00:17:03,272 --> 00:17:04,606
On my end,

247
00:17:06,358 --> 00:17:10,195
I know that no matter how much
you support me in my battles,

248
00:17:11,572 --> 00:17:14,199
you still worry so much about me.

249
00:17:15,367 --> 00:17:18,162
We almost lost each other
so many times before.

250
00:17:19,747 --> 00:17:22,708
[soft piano music continues playing]

251
00:17:34,636 --> 00:17:37,681
Mom, I'm sorry. I'm sorry, Mom.

252
00:17:38,515 --> 00:17:39,600
Hold on, Lily.

253
00:17:41,727 --> 00:17:44,188
You don't have to apologize
to me about anything.

254
00:17:45,939 --> 00:17:47,357
We both chose to do what's right,

255
00:17:47,441 --> 00:17:49,359
no matter how hard it is.

256
00:17:50,944 --> 00:17:54,573
No matter how many dragons
or demons we have to face,

257
00:17:55,240 --> 00:17:57,743
always remember
that I will be right beside you.

258
00:18:12,007 --> 00:18:15,010
[suspenseful music playing]

259
00:18:42,412 --> 00:18:44,581
Why are you so quiet, Emilia?

260
00:18:46,333 --> 00:18:49,753
Baby girl, baby girl,
baby girl. Baby girl?

261
00:18:50,712 --> 00:18:52,256
[exhales sharply] Emilia…

262
00:18:54,049 --> 00:18:56,301
I do not have time
for your issues right now.

263
00:19:06,103 --> 00:19:08,105
[Diego] <i>Diego, you</i>
<i>can't let them catch you.</i>

264
00:19:08,647 --> 00:19:11,108
<i>You have to find out where</i>
<i>they're keeping their guns.</i>

265
00:19:19,408 --> 00:19:20,742
Jan, you may leave.

266
00:19:36,884 --> 00:19:37,926
Excuse me, Madam.

267
00:19:38,802 --> 00:19:41,972
Jaguar has arrived.
The operation will now commence.

268
00:19:42,264 --> 00:19:43,182
Excellent.

269
00:19:43,265 --> 00:19:45,767
Wow, because of that,
you can live another day.

270
00:19:47,978 --> 00:19:48,979
Excuse me.

271
00:20:02,743 --> 00:20:05,746
[suspenseful music playing]

272
00:20:19,885 --> 00:20:21,094
[gunshots]

273
00:20:21,178 --> 00:20:22,846
[Damian] <i>You're here again, Fake Jaguar?!</i>

274
00:20:27,768 --> 00:20:30,395
[Camia] <i>If you stay here,</i>
<i>you can protect Lily</i>

275
00:20:30,479 --> 00:20:32,439
<i>and Lily can protect you,</i>

276
00:20:32,522 --> 00:20:35,067
<i>especially since you've already</i>
<i>left Red Dragon's syndicate.</i>

277
00:20:35,150 --> 00:20:38,028
<i>Damian, don't forget we all love you.</i>

278
00:20:38,779 --> 00:20:40,822
<i>We're ready to fight with you,</i>

279
00:20:40,906 --> 00:20:42,491
<i>as long as you stay true to us.</i>

280
00:20:44,117 --> 00:20:45,953
[Damian] You can get out of this, Damian.

281
00:20:46,411 --> 00:20:49,748
No one knows what happened. No one.

282
00:20:52,793 --> 00:20:55,837
[tense music playing]

283
00:21:03,762 --> 00:21:04,888
[exhales sharply]

284
00:21:24,741 --> 00:21:30,956
And this is how Helena Montoya
becomes Red Dragon.

285
00:21:33,041 --> 00:21:36,169
Is that the reason why you
changed your outfit to red,

286
00:21:36,253 --> 00:21:37,296
-Mama?
-Yes.

287
00:21:37,754 --> 00:21:38,797
Stunning!

288
00:21:40,299 --> 00:21:42,301
The wealth that sustains us,

289
00:21:43,135 --> 00:21:44,636
is the death of others.

290
00:21:47,973 --> 00:21:49,683
Are you listening to me, dear daughter?

291
00:21:50,976 --> 00:21:53,729
Dear daughter? Is that me, Mama?

292
00:21:54,604 --> 00:21:57,482
I'm getting confused
because you allowed Lily Cruz

293
00:21:57,566 --> 00:21:59,151
to call you "Mama."

294
00:21:59,234 --> 00:22:01,945
[sighs] So, we're actually
having this talk.

295
00:22:03,363 --> 00:22:05,574
Are you really jealous of Lily Cruz?

296
00:22:05,991 --> 00:22:07,159
Is it my fault?

297
00:22:07,951 --> 00:22:11,204
Did I not brief you on our plan of action?

298
00:22:12,539 --> 00:22:15,709
I know, Mama. You're just
luring her to your spider web.

299
00:22:16,126 --> 00:22:17,836
But you know, I can't help but notice.

300
00:22:18,211 --> 00:22:21,506
Something is different.
It seems different to me.

301
00:22:21,590 --> 00:22:24,760
It's not just an act of kindness
that you see in Lily Cruz.

302
00:22:25,052 --> 00:22:26,511
Something's different.

303
00:22:26,970 --> 00:22:29,056
Hmm… But I'm warning you, Mama,

304
00:22:30,265 --> 00:22:33,268
don't be fooled by her M.O.

305
00:22:33,894 --> 00:22:37,606
I should know because I fell
into her trap back then.

306
00:22:37,898 --> 00:22:39,524
You know what she did to me before, Mama?

307
00:22:39,941 --> 00:22:41,318
She got close to me

308
00:22:41,401 --> 00:22:43,570
and she almost took a bullet for my life.

309
00:22:43,945 --> 00:22:46,114
She saved my life. Exactly the same thing

310
00:22:46,198 --> 00:22:47,824
that she's doing to you right now, Mama.

311
00:22:48,116 --> 00:22:49,659
She saved your life, right?

312
00:22:49,743 --> 00:22:53,955
See what kind of person
our little "friend" is?

313
00:22:56,625 --> 00:22:58,627
[tense music playing]

314
00:23:02,631 --> 00:23:04,925
Mom, I think I need to help Diego.

315
00:23:06,051 --> 00:23:08,929
But you can't go into Helena's hideout.

316
00:23:09,012 --> 00:23:11,890
She can't find out that you know
she's Red Dragon.

317
00:23:17,813 --> 00:23:18,980
Hi, Jaguar.

318
00:23:20,190 --> 00:23:21,983
There's something
different about you tonight.

319
00:23:24,194 --> 00:23:27,114
Do you know how long
I've wanted to do this?

320
00:23:29,407 --> 00:23:30,408
[groans]

321
00:23:36,331 --> 00:23:40,377
Mom, I have to find a way
to help Diego's plan succeed.

322
00:23:41,878 --> 00:23:42,838
I'm sorry.

323
00:23:49,511 --> 00:23:51,513
[phone ringing]

324
00:23:53,140 --> 00:23:54,432
Speak of the devil.

325
00:23:54,766 --> 00:23:56,726
No, Mama. Don't! Don't.

326
00:23:56,810 --> 00:23:58,603
If what you say is true,

327
00:23:58,687 --> 00:24:00,397
I need to keep her close

328
00:24:01,106 --> 00:24:03,358
to see that chameleon's true colors.

329
00:24:03,441 --> 00:24:04,985
[phone continues ringing]

330
00:24:08,738 --> 00:24:10,157
Hello, Lily.

331
00:24:17,289 --> 00:24:20,125
This is what I like about you.
You don't give in so easily.

332
00:24:21,501 --> 00:24:22,878
[groans, grunts]

333
00:24:22,961 --> 00:24:24,254
Hold him steady!

334
00:24:27,674 --> 00:24:31,136
Aren't you tired of fantasizing
over that overgrown cat?!

335
00:24:32,345 --> 00:24:33,346
Enough!

336
00:24:34,389 --> 00:24:35,765
Get a move on, Jaguar!

337
00:24:37,934 --> 00:24:39,936
Mr. Yi is waiting.

338
00:24:53,950 --> 00:24:56,953
[soft music playing]

339
00:24:59,497 --> 00:25:00,498
Anna?

340
00:25:04,294 --> 00:25:06,963
Is something wrong? You look restless.

341
00:25:21,811 --> 00:25:22,812
[Natalie] <i>What?!</i>

342
00:25:24,022 --> 00:25:28,610
You mean to say
that Lily Cruz refused my help?

343
00:25:28,985 --> 00:25:30,278
Is she insane?

344
00:25:31,529 --> 00:25:33,406
I don't think she would do such a thing.

345
00:25:34,115 --> 00:25:38,620
She knows very well
that I have a lot of money

346
00:25:38,703 --> 00:25:40,205
and I have an army.

347
00:25:41,373 --> 00:25:43,625
I could probably be her best ally!

348
00:25:44,918 --> 00:25:47,629
So, Madrigal,
why don't you tell me the truth?

349
00:25:47,712 --> 00:25:52,550
Who doesn't want me
to join forces with Lily Cruz?

350
00:25:55,095 --> 00:25:56,096
Hmm?

351
00:25:58,181 --> 00:25:59,224
It's Anna.

352
00:25:59,724 --> 00:26:01,851
[scoffs] What?

353
00:26:09,943 --> 00:26:14,656
How can I know if what
I'm feeling is really love

354
00:26:14,739 --> 00:26:16,783
and not just something else?

355
00:26:18,785 --> 00:26:19,786
Well…

356
00:26:21,788 --> 00:26:24,624
Love does not delight in evil,
but rejoices in truth.

357
00:26:25,959 --> 00:26:28,670
It always protects, always trusts,

358
00:26:29,546 --> 00:26:33,258
always hopes, always perseveres.

359
00:26:34,175 --> 00:26:35,885
Love never fails.

360
00:26:38,471 --> 00:26:39,556
This is bad.

361
00:26:40,849 --> 00:26:42,934
Then it really is love.

362
00:26:51,234 --> 00:26:52,068
[scoffs]

363
00:26:52,152 --> 00:26:56,489
You mean to tell me
that this simple-minded,

364
00:26:57,073 --> 00:26:58,742
conniving little witch,

365
00:26:59,034 --> 00:27:00,994
who is a barrio girl, by the way,

366
00:27:02,078 --> 00:27:03,997
is sabotaging our plans?

367
00:27:04,539 --> 00:27:06,666
Natalie, don't think of her that way.

368
00:27:07,667 --> 00:27:08,918
We're just friends.

369
00:27:11,755 --> 00:27:15,216
So, you're siding with your friend?

370
00:27:16,134 --> 00:27:17,802
Is that what you're telling me?

371
00:27:20,221 --> 00:27:22,891
I'm getting tired of you listening to her.

372
00:27:25,310 --> 00:27:26,311
It's not funny.

373
00:27:27,354 --> 00:27:30,982
If you're not going to help me,
just leave.

374
00:27:31,983 --> 00:27:33,318
I don't need your help.

375
00:27:35,987 --> 00:27:37,322
I can handle myself.

376
00:27:38,740 --> 00:27:40,992
And just so you know, Madrigal…

377
00:27:42,243 --> 00:27:46,206
No matter what you do, you can't stop me.

378
00:27:54,381 --> 00:27:56,383
[suspenseful music playing]

379
00:27:57,217 --> 00:27:58,593
-Lily.
-Mama.

380
00:27:58,676 --> 00:27:59,928
What's the emergency?

381
00:28:01,304 --> 00:28:04,391
Nothing. Um. After what happened earlier,

382
00:28:04,474 --> 00:28:06,976
I just thought you might want to relax.

383
00:28:08,269 --> 00:28:09,270
So…

384
00:28:10,063 --> 00:28:12,357
For you, Mama. It's on me.

385
00:28:14,901 --> 00:28:16,444
You look stressed, Mama.

386
00:28:17,946 --> 00:28:19,739
How important is that…

387
00:28:20,907 --> 00:28:22,409
shipment of yours?

388
00:28:27,330 --> 00:28:28,706
How did you know about that?

389
00:28:32,001 --> 00:28:32,919
Well…

390
00:28:33,461 --> 00:28:35,255
During the medical mission,

391
00:28:35,505 --> 00:28:38,925
I kind of overheard you on the phone.

392
00:28:40,760 --> 00:28:42,887
Oh… that. [chuckles]

393
00:28:43,513 --> 00:28:44,639
Um,

394
00:28:44,723 --> 00:28:47,142
I'm still fixing
a few things here and there.

395
00:28:47,559 --> 00:28:49,728
But you're right. I do need a drink.

396
00:28:54,357 --> 00:28:55,650
Is this poisoned?

397
00:28:59,487 --> 00:29:00,864
I'm not like that.

398
00:29:02,157 --> 00:29:04,159
[suspenseful music playing]

399
00:29:06,786 --> 00:29:07,871
Cheers.

400
00:29:18,423 --> 00:29:19,549
You know the drill.

401
00:29:22,761 --> 00:29:24,137
Are we doing this all night?

402
00:29:25,930 --> 00:29:28,099
Jaguar, open the vault now!

403
00:29:29,350 --> 00:29:32,520
[suspenseful music playing]

404
00:29:47,535 --> 00:29:49,662
[both laugh]

405
00:29:50,914 --> 00:29:51,915
So, Mama,

406
00:29:52,332 --> 00:29:56,544
who among your clients
is giving you a headache?

407
00:29:57,295 --> 00:29:58,922
Well, let's see…

408
00:30:00,799 --> 00:30:02,967
There's this one. He's too specific.

409
00:30:04,010 --> 00:30:08,306
He wants to make sure that all
the pieces work in precision.

410
00:30:09,307 --> 00:30:12,727
He wants to strike everyone
who sees the product.

411
00:30:15,396 --> 00:30:17,732
[laughs]

412
00:30:23,863 --> 00:30:25,281
[suspenseful music playing]

413
00:30:25,824 --> 00:30:28,660
[buttons beeping]

414
00:30:31,871 --> 00:30:33,331
Strike everyone?

415
00:30:33,873 --> 00:30:36,042
Yes! Like a gunshot through the heart!

416
00:30:36,835 --> 00:30:40,380
Otherwise, why would I do all of this

417
00:30:41,047 --> 00:30:44,676
if it's not going to help
fund my projects, right?

418
00:30:45,593 --> 00:30:47,554
Including my creations.

419
00:30:48,721 --> 00:30:55,270
My products are meant
to strike any target.

420
00:30:57,230 --> 00:30:59,232
[beeps]

421
00:31:00,942 --> 00:31:02,277
Want a sample?

422
00:31:05,613 --> 00:31:06,573
Bang!

423
00:31:10,702 --> 00:31:16,332
[alarm blares]

424
00:31:19,043 --> 00:31:22,255
[both laugh]

425
00:31:26,634 --> 00:31:29,512
[alarm blaring]

426
00:31:44,819 --> 00:31:45,820
[gunshot]

427
00:31:49,490 --> 00:31:51,743
This is none of your business.

428
00:31:52,201 --> 00:31:53,786
You really are like the Madam.

429
00:31:55,121 --> 00:31:56,706
You people work too fast.

430
00:31:57,165 --> 00:31:59,125
I changed the vault's passcode last night.

431
00:32:22,899 --> 00:32:25,360
[tense music playing]

432
00:32:34,869 --> 00:32:37,038
[alarm blares]

433
00:33:01,813 --> 00:33:04,732
That's the problem with you,
Mercedes, you need to chill.

434
00:33:07,402 --> 00:33:10,071
Go ahead, Jaguar. Load it up.

435
00:33:11,364 --> 00:33:12,365
Boys.

436
00:33:18,121 --> 00:33:20,248
[tense music playing]

437
00:33:34,470 --> 00:33:35,471
Damian…

438
00:33:36,806 --> 00:33:37,849
Damian!

439
00:33:39,100 --> 00:33:41,811
What secret is Helena Montoya hiding?

440
00:33:43,396 --> 00:33:44,981
I don't know what you're talking about.

441
00:33:45,773 --> 00:33:48,317
I know there's something
you're not telling me.

442
00:33:49,527 --> 00:33:53,322
And I know you didn't come
with me and Lily back then

443
00:33:53,406 --> 00:33:55,658
because you're avoiding her.

444
00:33:56,075 --> 00:33:57,285
I got sick, remember?

445
00:33:58,286 --> 00:33:59,328
Damian…

446
00:34:00,997 --> 00:34:03,499
I don't want Lily to get hurt.

447
00:34:04,792 --> 00:34:08,004
So tell me if I should be worried!

448
00:34:08,713 --> 00:34:11,215
My daughter's going to meet
with Helena Montoya.

449
00:34:11,299 --> 00:34:12,884
Is she safe, Damian?

450
00:34:14,135 --> 00:34:15,386
Answer me!

451
00:34:15,470 --> 00:34:17,346
I don't know Helena Montoya.

452
00:34:26,439 --> 00:34:28,524
I know what you mean, Ma--

453
00:34:30,318 --> 00:34:31,235
Helena.

454
00:34:33,029 --> 00:34:35,448
Yes, that's right.

455
00:34:35,531 --> 00:34:37,492
And you know what? I…

456
00:34:37,575 --> 00:34:41,662
I really have always sensed
a connection between us.

457
00:34:43,039 --> 00:34:44,707
Oh, and speaking of shipment,

458
00:34:44,791 --> 00:34:47,460
I just have to make
one quick phone call, okay?

459
00:34:48,127 --> 00:34:50,004
-I'll be right back.
-Okay.

460
00:35:01,265 --> 00:35:04,060
[phone vibrates]

461
00:35:08,981 --> 00:35:10,900
We're moving the shipment to the truck.

462
00:35:11,526 --> 00:35:12,985
You know what to do.

463
00:35:13,069 --> 00:35:14,153
Yes.

464
00:35:14,237 --> 00:35:16,280
Mercedes, how's everything?

465
00:35:17,031 --> 00:35:19,242
Perfect. There's just one hiccup.

466
00:35:20,159 --> 00:35:20,952
What?

467
00:35:22,161 --> 00:35:23,162
Don't worry, Madam.

468
00:35:23,246 --> 00:35:25,998
Jaguar will deliver the shipment on time.

469
00:35:27,208 --> 00:35:28,126
Excellent.

470
00:35:28,918 --> 00:35:29,961
Be careful.

471
00:35:30,503 --> 00:35:31,546
I will.

472
00:35:49,230 --> 00:35:52,191
[suspenseful music playing]

473
00:36:04,954 --> 00:36:05,955
So…

474
00:36:06,455 --> 00:36:07,832
Where were we?

475
00:36:08,958 --> 00:36:09,959
Sit down.

476
00:36:10,585 --> 00:36:13,212
I'm sorry. I have a lot
of transactions myself.

477
00:36:13,796 --> 00:36:15,339
I know we're both busy people.

478
00:36:15,423 --> 00:36:18,217
But, you see? I make time for you.

479
00:36:19,051 --> 00:36:20,428
Should I be grateful?

480
00:36:21,387 --> 00:36:22,138
You should.

481
00:36:39,989 --> 00:36:41,240
[Julio] <i>Helena, I love you.</i>

482
00:36:41,991 --> 00:36:44,160
<i>Once I achieve my dream</i>
<i>of becoming president,</i>

483
00:36:46,996 --> 00:36:48,497
<i>you'll be my first lady.</i>

484
00:36:49,707 --> 00:36:51,000
[Helena] <i>Of course, Julio.</i>

485
00:36:52,001 --> 00:36:53,002
<i>I love you.</i>

486
00:36:54,128 --> 00:36:55,254
<i>I love you too, Helena.</i>

487
00:36:58,257 --> 00:37:00,927
<i>You whore! You lied to me!</i>

488
00:37:04,138 --> 00:37:04,889
<i>Damn!</i>

489
00:37:11,896 --> 00:37:15,691
<i>-Hello, ex-lover.</i>
<i>-Helena. You came back.</i>

490
00:37:17,610 --> 00:37:20,738
<i>I'm back. Well and alive.</i>

491
00:37:24,200 --> 00:37:27,745
[Julio] <i>So you want to play games, Helena?</i>

492
00:37:28,955 --> 00:37:32,959
<i>Fine. I'll join in on the fun.</i>

493
00:37:34,543 --> 00:37:40,883
<i>After all, I know just how much</i>
<i>of a sore loser you can be.</i>

494
00:37:42,218 --> 00:37:47,974
<i>And I can't wait to see</i>
<i>that look on your face again.</i>

495
00:38:03,656 --> 00:38:08,327
[Anna] <i>How can I know if what</i>
<i>I'm feeling is really love?</i>

496
00:38:09,161 --> 00:38:11,998
<i>Love does not delight in evil,</i>
<i>but rejoices in truth.</i>

497
00:38:13,249 --> 00:38:18,296
<i>It always protects,</i>
<i>always trusts, always hopes,</i>

498
00:38:19,130 --> 00:38:20,464
<i>always perseveres.</i>

499
00:38:21,215 --> 00:38:22,883
<i>Love never fails.</i>

500
00:38:26,554 --> 00:38:27,847
[Anna] <i>Cut it out, Anna.</i>

501
00:38:28,389 --> 00:38:29,890
<i>Just forget about your feelings.</i>

502
00:38:29,974 --> 00:38:31,726
<i>You're only going to get yourself hurt.</i>

503
00:38:32,727 --> 00:38:35,229
<i>Just accept the fact</i>
<i>that Jepoy likes someone else.</i>

504
00:38:35,313 --> 00:38:38,107
<i>It's not your fault he likes airheads.</i>

505
00:38:38,649 --> 00:38:40,484
<i>They deserve one another.</i>

506
00:38:53,664 --> 00:38:54,957
Anna, wait!

507
00:38:56,667 --> 00:38:59,754
[dramatic music playing]

508
00:39:03,758 --> 00:39:06,135
It's been 35 days.

509
00:39:06,719 --> 00:39:08,971
Hasn't that been long enough, Attorney?

510
00:39:09,055 --> 00:39:12,933
I thought you were expediting
my suspension.

511
00:39:13,768 --> 00:39:16,187
I did, Julio. But that's not the problem.

512
00:39:17,063 --> 00:39:19,106
But the charges of frustrated homicide

513
00:39:19,190 --> 00:39:21,942
that Camia Cruz pressed
against you are still in effect.

514
00:39:23,194 --> 00:39:27,156
So you're telling me that we
can work around my suspension,

515
00:39:27,615 --> 00:39:32,578
but that I still can't become
governor because of Camia Cruz?

516
00:39:33,496 --> 00:39:35,081
-Exactly.
-[scoffs]

517
00:39:36,457 --> 00:39:37,249
Colonel.

518
00:39:37,875 --> 00:39:41,295
Find out who all those witnesses were

519
00:39:41,545 --> 00:39:45,132
on the day I shot Camia Cruz.

520
00:39:45,216 --> 00:39:48,302
Let them know that they fired first,

521
00:39:48,386 --> 00:39:50,346
and that's why we fired back!

522
00:39:51,889 --> 00:39:52,765
Yes, sir.

523
00:39:54,892 --> 00:39:56,519
What do you plan to do next?

524
00:39:58,062 --> 00:40:01,816
I am going to solve a simple problem

525
00:40:01,899 --> 00:40:04,819
with an age-old solution

526
00:40:04,902 --> 00:40:08,072
so that I can get my position
as governor back,

527
00:40:08,739 --> 00:40:11,075
and rule this province once again.

528
00:40:11,534 --> 00:40:13,869
So please, Attorney, please…

529
00:40:14,120 --> 00:40:15,996
just attend to all these legalities

530
00:40:16,080 --> 00:40:17,915
and whatever else needs to be done

531
00:40:17,998 --> 00:40:20,918
so we can get all this nonsense over with.

532
00:40:21,710 --> 00:40:23,421
-Right away, sir.
-Yes, please.

533
00:40:27,633 --> 00:40:29,051
[exhales sharply]

534
00:40:37,143 --> 00:40:38,644
-Oh, Emilia.
-Papa.

535
00:40:41,480 --> 00:40:43,065
Where is your mother?

536
00:40:43,149 --> 00:40:45,151
I thought she was dropping by for dinner.

537
00:40:45,443 --> 00:40:47,319
She's having drinks with Lily Cruz.

538
00:40:47,778 --> 00:40:48,821
[scoffs]

539
00:40:50,239 --> 00:40:51,699
She stood us up for--

540
00:40:52,283 --> 00:40:54,326
You know what? This is all your fault.

541
00:40:54,743 --> 00:40:57,663
See? Even your own mother
doesn't want to be with you!

542
00:40:57,955 --> 00:40:59,081
[laughing]

543
00:40:59,165 --> 00:41:01,417
Mama has a plan.
So, if you want to pursue her,

544
00:41:01,500 --> 00:41:03,586
go to her directly, not through me.

545
00:41:04,003 --> 00:41:06,589
Besides, I'm not
your stupid cupid, you know?

546
00:41:06,964 --> 00:41:09,550
I'm not expecting this family
to ever become whole again

547
00:41:09,633 --> 00:41:12,011
because Mama doesn't need you,
and neither do I.

548
00:41:12,094 --> 00:41:13,387
We both don't need you!

549
00:41:16,974 --> 00:41:22,646
You are getting too big
for your breeches, Emilia.

550
00:41:23,063 --> 00:41:26,400
What are you so smug about, huh?
Your mother?

551
00:41:28,402 --> 00:41:29,778
Well, I've got news for you.

552
00:41:30,654 --> 00:41:33,115
Just because I'm not governor right now,

553
00:41:33,199 --> 00:41:35,201
doesn't mean you can treat me
like an old rag!

554
00:41:36,577 --> 00:41:41,373
Very soon, I am going to get
my governorship back.

555
00:41:42,208 --> 00:41:43,667
Sooner than you think!

556
00:41:44,668 --> 00:41:49,507
You and your mother will have to
take a backseat in this family.

557
00:41:50,633 --> 00:41:54,637
The two of you will pay
for all the disgrace

558
00:41:54,720 --> 00:41:57,014
and humiliation you've given me.

559
00:41:57,515 --> 00:41:58,516
[screams]

560
00:42:00,684 --> 00:42:01,644
[scoffs]

561
00:42:03,229 --> 00:42:05,147
You spoiled little brat.

562
00:42:18,410 --> 00:42:21,497
[tense music playing]

563
00:42:25,876 --> 00:42:28,337
Come back with the money
at exactly 10:00 p.m.

564
00:42:28,629 --> 00:42:30,798
Make sure it's the exact amount.

565
00:42:34,051 --> 00:42:35,177
I'll go with you.

566
00:42:37,638 --> 00:42:38,639
I can manage.

567
00:42:39,306 --> 00:42:41,308
You don't know where to deliver the goods.

568
00:42:42,142 --> 00:42:43,352
Just leave it to me.

569
00:42:45,437 --> 00:42:47,731
If you really know, tell us.

570
00:42:50,317 --> 00:42:51,402
That's not necessary.

571
00:42:57,825 --> 00:42:59,243
You know what to do with him.

572
00:43:04,081 --> 00:43:06,125
[suspenseful music playing]

573
00:43:11,839 --> 00:43:13,507
[groans, grunts]

574
00:43:13,591 --> 00:43:14,800
Don't let him escape!

575
00:43:19,972 --> 00:43:22,099
Well, Lily, I think it's time
for me to go.

576
00:43:22,182 --> 00:43:25,144
I'm not a young 'un anymore.
I can't stay up late.

577
00:43:25,227 --> 00:43:28,188
Besides, I must oversee the shipment.

578
00:43:28,272 --> 00:43:29,064
[phone rings]

579
00:43:29,148 --> 00:43:30,774
Oh, here's an update.

580
00:43:33,110 --> 00:43:35,112
[phone continues ringing]

581
00:43:36,196 --> 00:43:38,157
What is the meaning of this?

582
00:43:40,701 --> 00:43:43,662
Didn't we say… no phones?

583
00:43:44,913 --> 00:43:46,874
We said no such things.

584
00:43:52,129 --> 00:43:54,131
[tense music playing]

585
00:44:02,806 --> 00:44:04,475
Come on, Helena.

586
00:44:16,570 --> 00:44:17,821
[grunts]

587
00:44:30,334 --> 00:44:33,337
You can ignore your own daughter,

588
00:44:34,546 --> 00:44:35,673
but not me.

589
00:44:38,884 --> 00:44:40,135
Not me.

590
00:44:48,894 --> 00:44:54,191
<i>More than a thousand firearms</i>
<i>amounting to 50 million pesos</i>

591
00:44:54,274 --> 00:44:57,861
<i>are currently in police custody</i>
<i>after being seized</i>

592
00:44:57,945 --> 00:44:59,446
<i>from a shipment made by Red Dragon.</i>

593
00:44:59,530 --> 00:45:00,739
<i>The fight continues, Mom.</i>

594
00:45:00,823 --> 00:45:02,783
<i>Am I going to have someone buried soon?</i>

595
00:45:02,866 --> 00:45:03,742
<i>Yes.</i>

596
00:45:03,826 --> 00:45:05,828
<i>I'm done playing games with Red Dragon.</i>

597
00:45:05,911 --> 00:45:07,579
<i>I've lost my patience.</i>

598
00:45:07,663 --> 00:45:10,082
[Julio] <i>Julio Ardiente is still</i>

599
00:45:10,165 --> 00:45:13,335
<i>king of the province of Ardiente.</i>

600
00:45:15,129 --> 00:45:17,047
<i>Diego's pretending to be Jaguar.</i>

601
00:45:17,131 --> 00:45:18,424
[Diego] <i>As long as I'm alive,</i>

602
00:45:18,507 --> 00:45:21,301
<i>you'll never be the governor</i>
<i>of this province.</i>

603
00:45:21,385 --> 00:45:24,388
[theme music playing]
